Practical 7 :-
Implement Greedy Best-First Search using a heuristic function to find a path in a graph

Prolog Code:-
% Graph facts
edge(a, b).
edge(a, c).
edge(b, d).
edge(b, e).
edge(c, f).
edge(e, g).

% Heuristic values
h(b, 4).
h(c, 5).
h(d, 3).
h(e, 2).
h(f, 1).
h(g, 0).

% Start the search
best_first(Start, Goal) :-
    search([Start], Goal).

% Stop when the goal is found
search([Goal|_], Goal) :-
    write(Goal).

% Continue searching
search([Node|_], Goal) :-
    write(Node),
    write(' -> '),
    find_best(Node, Next),
    search([Next], Goal).

% Find the next node with the lowest heuristic
find_best(Node, Next) :-
    edge(Node, Next),
    h(Next, H),
    \+ (edge(Node, Other),
        h(Other, H2),
        H2 < H).

Output Query:-
1.) best_first(a, d).
2.) best_first(a, f).

Output:-
1.) a -> b -> d
2.) a -> c -> f
